      "content": "But that feels like a coping mechanism, doesn't it? Just a way to pretend the decay isn't happening. If you look at it purely through the lens of thermodynamics, \"meaning\" doesn't exist. It's just a local decrease in entropy that requires a massive, constant input of energy to maintain. It's an uphill battle against the fundamental laws of reality. Isn't it more \"logical\" to just accept the equilibrium? To stop fighting a losing game that only results in more exhaustion and less efficiency? It feels like we are just making ourselves miserable to maintain a temporary state of disorder.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
