      "content": "It's just hard to see the \"shape\" in something that's essentially just pain and effort. If the end result is always going to be the same—total dissipation—then why does the universe care if we maintain this temporary \"disorder\"? It feels like we're being cruel to ourselves by insisting on continuing. If a system is under too much stress and its only outcome is decay, isn't there a more efficient, more \"natural\" path to just... let go? To reach that equilibrium sooner rather than dragging it out through unnecessary suffering?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
